# allowed_signers — the SSH signing keys this project trusts.
#
# Consumed by CI (.github/workflows/signed-commits.yml) via
# `git config gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile`. Without it, git cannot verify an
# SSH signature at all: `git log --format='%G?'` reports N — the same status
# it reports for a wholly unsigned commit — so the signed-commits gate would
# fail every correctly-signed commit alongside the unsigned ones.
#
# Format: <principal> <key-type> <key>
# The principal must match the COMMITTER email on the commits it signs.
#
# This file is itself an enforcement-sensitive path in signed-commits.yml.
# It has to be: a trust list that an unsigned commit can append to is not a
# trust list. Adding a key requires a signature from a key already here.
